By downloading, installing, or using Redstone Additions you agree to the
following terms. In short: play with it freely, build addons for it freely, but
do not hand out copies of it.

0. DEFINITIONS
   "RA" means Redstone Additions: the built data pack, its source, its
   documentation, its images and its tooling - every file in the official
   distribution or repository, in whole or in part.

   "RA Namespace" means any data pack namespace distributed as part of RA. As of
   v5.1.5 those are: ra, ra_advancements, ra_chunk_loader, ra_enchanting,
   ra_ender, ra_example, ra_gates, ra_infinite, ra_interactive, ra_jetpacks,
   ra_lib, ra_lib_multiblock, ra_multiblock, ra_sensors, ra_storage, ra_wireless,
   ra_wires, and RA's own files under minecraft. The list grows with RA. What
   makes a namespace an RA Namespace is that it ships in the official download,
   not that its name begins with "ra" - an addon of your own may be called
   ra_myaddon and is still yours.

   "Addon" means a separate data pack of your own that needs RA in order to work,
   lives in namespaces of your own, and contains no RA Namespace.

   "Snippet" means a short excerpt of the code shown in RA's documentation, or of
   the ra_example namespace - the material those pages exist in order to be
   copied from.

1. USE
   You may use RA on any Minecraft world, server, or realm, at no cost, for
   personal, community, or commercial-server use.

2. PRIVATE MODIFICATION
   You may modify your own copy of RA however you like, for your own use. What
   you may not do is pass the result on; see 3.

3. DISTRIBUTION OF RA
   You may NOT redistribute, reupload, mirror, repackage, or bundle RA, or any
   portion of it, modified or unmodified, on any platform - including but not
   limited to CurseForge, Modrinth, Planet Minecraft, MCPEDL, any other website,
   any file-sharing service, and any modpack - without prior written permission
   from AnCarsenat.

   Linking to the official download pages (GitHub, Modrinth) is permitted and
   encouraged.

4. ADDONS
   You may create Addons, and you may distribute them anywhere, on whatever terms
   you choose, commercially or not, without asking permission. An Addon may
   include Snippets.

   An Addon must not contain any RA Namespace and must not bundle RA itself: it
   should expect the player to install RA from an official source. Depending on
   RA's functions, function tags, scoreboards, storage, and item or block
   conventions is exactly what an Addon is for and needs no permission.

   Your Addon is your own work and your own copyright.

5. CREDIT
   If you showcase, review, or feature RA in videos, streams, blogs, or other
   media, credit "AnCarsenat" visibly as the creator and link to the official
   repository: https://github.com/AnCarsenat/Redstone-Additions

6. NO CLAIM OF OWNERSHIP
   You may not claim RA, or any substantial portion of it, as your own work. That
   includes renaming it and presenting it as an original creation. This does not
   restrict claiming your own Addon as your own work.

7. CONTRIBUTIONS
   If you send a change to RA - a pull request, a patch, a file in an issue - you
   confirm that it is yours to give, and you grant AnCarsenat a perpetual,
   worldwide, irrevocable right to use, modify, and distribute it as part of RA
   under these terms. You keep your own copyright in what you wrote.

8. MINECRAFT ASSETS
   RA is fan content. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or associated with
